<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia sets base price for olive oil exports.</title>
<headline>Tunisia sets base price for olive oil exports.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia on Friday announced that it has set for the first time a base price for olive oil exports during the 1996/1997 season.</p>
<p>Agriculture Minister Mohamed Ben Rejeb said the minimum price for exports of olive oil by the private sector was set at 2,900 dinars ($2,959) per tonne.</p>
<p>Ben Rejeb said olive oil output was expected to exceed 200,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The olive oil season starts on November 15.  </p>
<p>Output will be sharply above last season's 60,000 tonnes.</p>
</text>
